win32u: Keep vkd3d presentation ahead of competing surfaces for the same HWND.

After Effects 26.5 presents its composition through vkd3d D3D12, but also
presents a D3D11/DXVK surface to the same HWND. Copying both client surfaces
into the toplevel lets the legacy target cover the composition with black
when the timeline is hovered or the viewer is clicked.

Identify vkd3d through its Vulkan engine name. After a successful present,
retain that client surface as the window's presentation owner. Other client
surfaces for that HWND cannot overwrite it until the owning swapchain or
surface is destroyed. A private window property tracks ownership without
changing the graphics-driver ABI or adding launcher configuration.

This is a targeted vkd3d compatibility rule, not a general composition model
for arbitrarily layered graphics APIs. Microsoft discourages combining flip
presentation and other APIs in one HWND; Windows reference testing and broader
Adobe regression coverage remain necessary before general deployment.

Reproducer: tests/d3d12child/d3d12child.c -underlay. With the original runtime,
the user observes black then green. With this patch: retained red then green
when the D3D12 swapchain is released. Tested on Wine 11.20, X11/Hyprland,
NVIDIA RTX 3060. See docs/MISTER-HORSE.md for application validation.

